{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a9003b8b-34c9-47b5-83f2-6480bdcaa939","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1739d9e04774fd9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-rcfwetod/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# KServe serving-stack image FIPS 140-3 conversion\n\n## Description\n\nConverts the KServe component's serving-stack images so they run correctly on\nFIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no\nnon-validated crypto in the request path. This epic also produces the crypto\nmodule inventory, build attestations, and test results for the KServe images\n(inputs to the compliance evidence package) and wires a gating CI check that\nprevents FIPS regressions in KServe builds.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all KServe serving-stack images for linked cryptographic libraries;\n  classify each as validated or non-validated and record the result as a\n  per-image module inventory (the strategy does not enumerate the affected\n  images — this audit produces the definitive list).\n- Replace or rebuild non-validated crypto usage so the images run on\n  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated modules; the request path must contain\n  no non-validated crypto.\n- Verify correct runtime behavior of the converted images on FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift clusters (inference request serving, InferenceService status\n  handling).\n- Add a gating CI check to the KServe build pipeline that fails any\n  serving-stack build reintroducing non-validated crypto usage, and verify the\n  check passes on the converted images and fails on a deliberately\n  non-compliant build.\n- Keep the KServe build pipeline green after the conversion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every KServe serving-stack image in scope runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift cluster and uses validated cryptographic modules, with no\n  non-validated crypto in the request path.\n- A module inventory exists for every KServe image in scope, classifying each\n  linked crypto library as validated or non-validated, in a form suitable for\n  inclusion in the compliance evidence package.\n- Build attestations and FIPS test results for the converted KServe images\n  are produced and available to the compliance evidence package.\n- A gating CI check fails any KServe serving-stack build that reintroduces\n  non-validated crypto usage, and passes on the converted images.\n- The KServe build pipeline is green for the converted images.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): the KServe share of \"all serving-stack images run correctly on\n  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto\n  in the request path)\".\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the FIPS regression gating check for KServe builds is\n  delivered here rather than as a separate epic — it enforces the same build\n  surfaces this epic converts, so it is not independently deferrable and\n  splitting it would require a second wiring pass over the same pipelines.\n- HLR-2 (P0, slice): module inventory, build attestations, and test results\n  for the KServe images, aggregated into the compliance evidence package by\n  the evidence/submission work.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Specific remediation choices (which validated modules replace which\n  libraries, per-language crypto provider configuration) are implementation\n  decisions for the team; the strategy deliberately leaves them open.\n- If the image audit materially exceeds the strategy's \"several images\"\n  estimate, re-scope before continuing.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40908,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87c493d1e6459024","agent_id":"a7e62c1559cd8ac23","session_id":"c0af6202-03d2-4ad7-8476-de2ac99e02dd","uuid":"b1415144-cc3e-43a1-9926-92759d1d0416","timestam