n- Consumes the HLR-1 deliverables (converted images and their per-image\n  evidence inputs) from the conversion work.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The accredited lab's historical turnaround is six to nine months, and the\n  security review board meets on its own cadence; both are externally\n  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They dominate the\n  schedule and belong in delivery planning, not in this epic's acceptance\n  criteria.\n- The certification grant itself is the lab's decision; this epic's completion\n  point is the assembled, review-board-triaged, lab-delivered package.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42661,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87c493d1e6459024","agent_id":"a7e62c1559cd8ac23","session_id":"c0af6202-03d2-4ad7-8476-de2ac99e02dd","uuid":"382aeda5-4e08-4153-9e8c-687fbb57b1de","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:10:45.297Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
