{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-989c9a6805605039","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: KServe serving-stack image FIPS 140-3 conversion\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# KServe serving-stack image FIPS 140-3 conversion\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tConverts the KServe component's serving-stack images so they run correctly on\n34\tFIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no\n35\tnon-validated crypto in the request path. This epic also produces the crypto\n36\tmodule inventory, build attestations, and test results for the KServe images\n37\t(inputs to the compliance evidence package) and wires a gating CI check that\n38\tprevents FIPS regressions in KServe builds.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit all KServe serving-stack images for linked cryptographic libraries;\n43\t  classify each as validated or non-validated and record the result as a\n44\t  per-image module inventory (the strategy does not enumerate the affected\n45\t  images — this audit produces the definitive list).\n46\t- Replace or rebuild non-validated crypto usage so the images run on\n47\t  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated modules; the request path must contain\n48\t  no non-validated crypto.\n49\t- Verify correct runtime behavior of the converted images on FIPS-enabled\n50\t  OpenShift clusters (inference request serving, InferenceService status\n51\t  handling).\n52\t- Add a gating CI check to the KServe build pipeline that fails any\n53\t  serving-stack build reintroducing non-validated crypto usage, and verify the\n54\t  check passes on the converted images and fails on a deliberately\n55\t  non-compliant build.\n56\t- Keep the KServe build pipeline green after the conversion.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Every KServe serving-stack image in scope runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n61\t  OpenShift cluster and uses validated cryptographic modules, with no\n62\t  non-validated crypto in the request path.\n63\t- A module inventory exists for every KServe image in scope, classifying each\n64\t  linked crypto library as validated or non-validated, in a form suitable for\n65\t  inclusion in the compliance evidence package.\n66\t- Build attestations and FIPS test results for the converted KServe images\n67\t  are produced and available to the compliance evidence package.\n68\t- A gating CI check fails any KServe serving-stack build that reintroduces\n69\t  non-validated crypto usage, and passes on the converted images.\n70\t- The KServe build pipeline is green for the converted images.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-1 (P0): the KServe share of \"all serving-stack images run correctly on\n75\t  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto\n76\t  in the request path)\".\n77\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the FIPS regression gating check for KServe builds is\n78\t  delivered here rather than as a separate epic — it enforces the same build\n79\t  surfaces this epic converts, so it is not independently deferrable and\n80\t  splitting it would require a second wiring pass over the same pipelines.\n81\t- HLR-2 (P0, slice): module inventory, build attestations, and test results\n82\t  for the KServe images, aggregated into the compliance evidence package by\n83\t  the evidence/submission work.\n84\t\n85\t## Risks / Notes\n86\t\n87\t- Specific remediation choices (which validated modules replace which\n88\t  libraries, per-language crypto provider configuration) are implementation\n89\t  decisions for the team; the strategy deliberately leaves them open.\n90\t- If the image audit materially exceeds the strategy's \"several images\"\n91\t  estimate, re-scope before continuing.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-893f1b092e44f041","agent_id":"a942642b9696894a4","session_id":"c0af6202-03d2-4ad7-8476-de2ac99e02dd","uuid":"72709a31-1911-4871-b263-203f40e9c123","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:12:43.944Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-989c9a6805605039","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
