ven if it uses the word \"available\". Flag each misfiled AC as an issue (severity minor) with the correction \"move to Risks/Notes\". Also check that epic bodies do not reference sibling epics by draft ID (e.g., \"E001\", \"E003\") — draft IDs are meaningless in Jira. Each reference is a minor issue; 3+ across the decomposition costs a point.\nskills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:146:23. Strategy replaces existing capability → add rollback/feature-flag AC to replacing Implementation epic\nskills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:248:- Implementation-specific requirements (build pipeline green, rollback plan, doc review, etc.)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-893f1b092e44f041","agent_id":"a942642b9696894a4","session_id":"c0af6202-03d2-4ad7-8476-de2ac99e02dd","uuid":"4cddabed-c7c1-4fca-8c48-49a34acc2462","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:15:00.689Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87052db34c9c7190","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
